214	// isContextKill reports whether waitErr looks like exec.CommandContext's kill
215	// triggered by ctx being done (signal termination while ctx.Err() is set), as
216	// opposed to the CLI exiting on its own. On Windows a context kill reports a
217	// normal exit code, so this returns false there and real process failures keep
218	// their precedence over a decoded result.
